# Build context for the application images. Keep it small: a large context slows every build and can
# leak local state into a layer. The context is the repository root because the demo API is part of the
# single Python project and the frontend is an npm workspace whose dependencies are hoisted.
#
# Never excluded, because the builds need them:
#   pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md, LICENSE   (Python project metadata)
#   package.json, package-lock.json, tsconfig.base.json
#   packages/, services/, scripts/, apps/demo-app/frontend/

# Version control and editor state
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Secrets and local configuration: these must never reach an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig

# Python local state
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov

# Node local state and build output
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Infrastructure, observability and documentation: validated by their own tools, unused by the builds
infra
observability
docs
tests
AI_Native_DevOps_SRE_DataFactor_Agentic_Task_List.md
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
SECURITY.md
Makefile
compose*.yaml
compose*.yml

# Terraform state, plans and downloaded providers (never in an image)
**/.terraform
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.json
.terraform.lock.hcl
